        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n4 3\n1 3 2 4\n4 3 2 1\n1 1\n2 3 1\n1 2",
        "output": "4\n2\n8",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1:\n\nRami's permutation is (1,3,2,4)→(3,2,4,1)→(3,2,4,1)→(4,1,3,2)(1, 3, 2, 4) \\rightarrow (3, 2, 4, 1) \\rightarrow (3, 2, 4, 1) \\rightarrow (4, 1, 3, 2)(1,3,2,4)→(3,2,4,1)→(3,2,4,1)→(4,1,3,2).\nGhoda's permutation is (4,3,2,1)→(4,3,2,1)→(2,3,4,1)→(2,3,4,1)(4, 3, 2, 1) \\rightarrow (4, 3, 2, 1) \\rightarrow (2, 3, 4, 1) \\rightarrow (2, 3, 4, 1)(4,3,2,1)→(4,3,2,1)→(2,3,4,1)→(2,3,4,1)."
      }
